    thinking: "**Debugging Server Configuration**\n\nI\'ve been troubleshooting the `server_console.log` file creation. Initially, I suspected a discrepancy in `process.cwd()` between server environments. Now, I see the root cause! The issue is in `server.ts` on line 700: a `supabase` call may be the problem.\n\n\n**Isolating the Error Source**\n\nI\'ve homed in on a potential vulnerability: the absence of error handling in the `memorial_versions` insertion. A failed database write here could cause an unhandled promise rejection, which causes the express route handler to return an internal server error. While there is a `try...catch` block higher up, I now think it doesn\'t catch the error in this specific location. This is an important gap in the logic!\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
