    thinking: "**Analyzing Data Flow**\n\nOkay, so I\'m seeing the expected zero from anon, good. The `SaasGerarBiografia.tsx` file is sending an empty `respostas` array when Role-Level Security hides them. I\'m now digging into `server.ts` to see how it\'s processing this potentially empty data.\n\n\n**Investigating Data Integrity**\n\nI\'ve discovered the server completely overrides the `respostas` data. It seems the issue isn\'t empty arrays, but possibly data integrity, given a previous log of empty responses. The server retrieves answers using the Service Role Key, meaning if data exists on the backend, the API call should find it. I\'m checking why Claude API might be receiving only generic placeholder text. Could it be a data population problem?\n\n\n**Unraveling Claude\'s Behavior**\n\nI\'ve hit a key point: Claude\'s refusal to generate biographies, signified by \"Avalie: Qual caminho voc\303\252 prefere?\", points to garbage input. This triggers Markdown text. The UI handles the refusal gracefully, displaying a message about generic filler text. The user can still proceed to generate audio. Now I must see what happens after clicking the \"Aprovar e Gerar \303\201udio\" button, where `/api/narrativas/audio` comes into play.\n\n\n"
